pert ratings.", "Incumbent Jeff Van Drew (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Incumbent Republican Jeff Van Drew seeks another term in New Jersey's second district, a seat with a five-point Republican lean that he flipped in 2018 and has held since as a Republican. He faces Democratic nominee Zack Mullock, a local councilman who won the June primary. Van Drew holds a commanding financial edge, with roughly $1.5 million on hand compared with about $120,000 for Mullock, and no significant outside spending has appeared on either side.\n\nExpert raters overwhelmingly place the race in the Likely or Safe Republican column, and prediction markets give Van Drew roughly an 83 percent chance of winning. The lone available poll, a Democratic-sponsored survey from May 2025, showed Van Drew ahead by ten points, though it is dated and hypothetical. The race appears Van Drew's to lose, with the main question being the size of his victory margin rather than the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1228, "margin": -7.28}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1056, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1079, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0906, "margin": -9.0}]}